    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` derived field on the owner response, mapping the locality/region to an IANA timezone name via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`LocalityLookup.java`** \u2014 added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table and a `timezoneForCustomerCode(customerCode, postcode, city)` method that reuses the existing region-derivation logic (`forCustomerCode`) and maps the resulting region through the table. Regions not in the table (including `\"UNKNOWN\"`) yield `null`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `timezone` that calls the new lookup method, mirroring the existing `locality` mapping.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` property to the owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`) passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
